content.text:
The independent redraft is now complete. It gives the exact amendments needed before code:

- immutable `IntentDigest` binding intent, state, receipt, resume, and reconciliation;
- a qualified release identity that cannot deserialize a bare package;
- an explicit, canonical operation DAG;
- a complete graph-built `ReleaseInputSnapshotV1`;
- persisted `Pending → Attempting → terminal` transitions, with no blind retry after interruption;
- per-operation final precondition checks and an execution lock;
- durable failures with no arbitrary text;
- an explicit migration boundary so old `PublishPlan + ApplyPermit` routes cannot bypass validated execution;
- explicit Git-commit versus hermetic-content trust profiles.

I’m applying those amendments to the foundation and will re-run the same independent gates before allowing planning or code to begin.

